{{also|Wenn|wénn}}
==German==

===Etymology===
Like {{m|de|wann}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*hwannē||at what time, when}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*kʷo-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kʷi-||interrogative base}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/vɛn/}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-wenn.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{audio|de|De-wenn.ogg}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|de|conjunction|cat2=subordinating conjunctions|subordinating}}

# [[when]], [[whenever]]
#: {{ux|de|Sag bitte Bescheid, wenn du fertig bist!|translation=Tell me when you're done!}}
# [[if]] {{gloss|on the condition that}}
#: {{ux|de|Was tun, '''wenn''' ich nicht weiß, ob sie mich liebt?|translation=What (to do) '''if''' I don't know if she loves me?}}

====Usage notes====
Instead of using ''wenn'' to introduce a conditional clause, verb-initial (V1) word order can also be used:
: {{ux|de|Wird das nicht gemacht, müsste die Nutzung beschränkt werden.|translation=(If) that is not done, then the uses will have to be limited.}}
In any case, the main clause can, but need not be, introduced by ''dann'' or ''so'':
: {{ux|de|Bedenkt man, dass Gold recht schwer zu finden ist, so/dann ist es kein Wunder, dass es so wertvoll ist.|translation=If we consider that gold is rather difficult to come by, it is no wonder that it is so valuable.}}
: {{ux|de|[[wenn man vom Teufel spricht, kommt er|Wenn man vom Teufel spricht, kommt er]].|translation=[[speak of the devil and he shall appear|Speak of the devil and he shall appear]].}}

